{
  "_comment": [
    "Kernels CI builds (sfs/build.sh <tag>). Each target is a GKI release tag of kernel/common,",
    "i.e. a kernel Google shipped: building the very release a device runs keeps its stock",
    "modules' CRCs matching. manifest is the kernel/manifest branch of that release, for a",
    "toolchain and Kleaf of the same era. fixups names a set in sfs/patches/fixup_susfs.py that",
    "makes susfs4ksu's patch apply with --fuzz=0. 6.12 builds without LTO like its official GKI",
    "(with LTO, Kconfig drops RUST and rust_binder.ko); 6.1 and 6.6 use thin LTO.",
    "The Manager recommends the build whose kernel version matches the device (or the closest)."
  ],
